<title>USA: Rockwell Automotive sees profit growth.</title>
<headline>Rockwell Automotive sees profit growth.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rockwell International Corp's soon-to-be-independent automotive business expects to achieve average annual profit growth of about 15 percent over the next five years, company officials said Monday.</p>
<p>At a Detroit news conference, Larry Yost, designated president of the automotive operations, said the company expects sales growth averaging six percent for the heavy truck components business and eight percent for the light vehicle components business.</p>
</text>
